From 6721503d6021a54b6fbea0bd2cb561368a24e326 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:51:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] A finished remote card stays released when its owner
 goes silent after publishing it

Problem: a session panel listed completed cards as "status unknown
(missing qualified identity)" after their owners stopped. Closed cards remained
unfinished obligations (`done_pending_release` / `unknown`, reported_status done or archived).

Why 1: `replica_cards` lists an unreleased link to a closed card; the links were unreleased because the reconciler's
ledger projection (`_ledger_links` <- `_remote_links`) said `released: False` for them.
Why 2: `owner_attests_terminal` releases a terminal record only while the owner's scope heartbeat is inside its
freshness window at read time. The example workers had been shut down;
their last beats were outside the freshness window.
Why 3: the verdict is recomputed on every read and nothing remembers that the owner attested the record while it
was alive, so an owner going silent un-released its previously finished terminal records, each of
them hash-attested and published before the owner's last beat).
Root (happened): the freshness window was written to stop an offline owner's last word being read as current, and
was applied to records the owner had already stood behind with a later clean read of the same scope.
Root (not caught): the tests pinned the expiry itself (`test_expiry_flips_release_exactly_after_the_window`) with a
record published at the very instant of the beat, and no test shut an owner down after it had finished cards.

Fix: a terminal, hash-attested owner record published at or before the owner's LAST clean read of its scope stays
released while the owner is silent (`kanban_scope_heartbeat.published_before_silence`; publication time = the
replica row's `updated_at`). Unchanged: a record published after the last beat, an owner that never beat, a scope
the collector could not read, a future-dated beat and a stale hub sync release nothing; a returning owner that
publishes the card open again un-releases it; ledger-bound cards still need verified completion evidence.
- `fresh_scopes` returns `ScopeVerdicts`: the fresh scopes plus each quiet scope's last beat, equal and hashed on
  both, so the memoized and incremental projections rebuild when a scope goes quiet or beats again and reuse while
  it stays silent. `live_scopes` stays a plain frozenset of fresh scopes.
- `owner_attests_terminal(..., published_at=)` (full projection), `kanban_replica_projection._apply` and the
  bystander `EvidenceSet` (incremental) apply the same rule; the narrow annotation key keeps a quiet owner's clock.
- The origin-ledger path (`kanban_origin_ledger`, `via: origin`) is not changed.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_release_survives_owner_silence.py (the pure rule; ScopeVerdicts keying;
owner_attests_terminal; the explicit-now full read and the memoized live read on one replica file agree: silent
owner keeps done and archived cards published at or before its last beat, not one published after; returning
owner reopening; stale hub; no heartbeat; unreadable scope). test_kanban_replica_read_memo_heartbeat.py::
test_expiry_flips_release_exactly_after_the_window now publishes its card after the last beat, which is the case
the expiry still governs. Source tests cover the affected modules. A projection check verifies
that completed and archived shepherd links remain released after an owner goes silent;
open cards remain unreleased. Untested: the Desktop render and
remembered snapshot rows whose records the replica no longer carries (unchanged here).

